{"title":"2016 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2c","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2016 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>When Esther and her older brother Paul race, Esther takes 5 steps every 2 seconds, and each of her steps is 0.4 m long. Paul also takes 5 steps every 2 seconds, but each of his steps is 1.2 m long.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If they both start a race at the same time, what distance ahead will Paul be after 2 minutes?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> seconds are in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> minute. Since both of them take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> steps every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> seconds, they would take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/c/64c9c2976c5478cebed6d470f3a1dad8398cfdb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\times 60 = 300$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" /> steps in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> minutes.\n</p><p>Each of Paul's steps is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/1/8e14f624aafae782a8e94b168073c9b91ecea7bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.2 - 0.4 = 0.8 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"137\" height=\"15\" /> longer than each of Esther's steps. \n</p><p>Thus, Paul would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/c/45c5899be0353df9c3b623cde75421a21b70ed11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$300 \\times 0.8 = \\boxed{240 \\text{ m}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"157\" height=\"25\" /> ahead of Esther.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2b\" title=\"2016 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2b\">part b</a>, we know that Paul's speed is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/e/46e105bd69c5c00ef0689baa46bc116244cc728a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\frac{\\text{m}}{\\text{s}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"29\" height=\"34\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> minutes is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/1/76158b568964e34bf8ce620bf44e8e7df629ed8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 60 = 120 \\text{ s}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"115\" height=\"15\" />, so Paul travels <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/5/c451c776b4a5a62354175bd15d1a2b120836500d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\times 120 = 360 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"131\" height=\"15\" /> in total.\n</p><p>From <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2a\" title=\"2016 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2a\">part a</a>, Esther travels <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/4/7e4df42ce5fc073e740457a4caa30765f87d2a4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> seconds. Since there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> seconds in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> minute, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> seconds is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/6/8f60bedc5b5b46bbd2652971d30b4e69bfad748a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{60}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> minutes, and so she travels <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/0/210d0353eed5d957dc2c38eba2cd982d04ded337.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 60 = 120 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"122\" height=\"15\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> minutes.\n</p><p>Thus, Paul would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/a/88a33bcb47420bcef6b85f31ba817e0c02561e56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$360 - 120 = \\boxed{240 \\text{ m}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"161\" height=\"25\" /> ahead of Esther.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2b\" title=\"2016 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2b\">part b</a>, we know that Paul's speed is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/e/46e105bd69c5c00ef0689baa46bc116244cc728a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\frac{\\text{m}}{\\text{s}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"29\" height=\"34\" />. Additionally, from <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2a\" title=\"2016 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2a\">part a</a>, Esther travels <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/4/7e4df42ce5fc073e740457a4caa30765f87d2a4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> seconds. This means that Esther's speed is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/e/85edf2a2ce22eb7627c14bd5e9a51cf4e5bfb0a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{2} = 1 \\frac{\\text{m}}{\\text{s}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"66\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>The difference between the speeds is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/5/d357f7cff37729c2bac3b42f43e1e442be72175c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 - 1 = 2 \\frac{\\text{m}}{\\text{s}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"93\" height=\"34\" />, meaning that every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/0/340cba9564f91327008dcb44148e800a1860e2f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\text{ s}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"23\" height=\"14\" />, Paul becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/4/7e4df42ce5fc073e740457a4caa30765f87d2a4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> more ahead. \n</p><p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> seconds in a minute, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> minutes is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/1/76158b568964e34bf8ce620bf44e8e7df629ed8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 60 = 120 \\text{ s}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"115\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, Paul would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/2/2224450bbad65fc23294b9d9bf272809852f23b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 120 = \\boxed{240 \\text{ m}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"143\" height=\"25\" /> ahead of Esther.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018002017\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.022 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.098 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 161/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 279/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6086/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.726      1 2016_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2\n100.00%    6.726      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36958:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018002017 and revision id 285846. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}